; rippledd.dll: the moose-ripple DirectDraw HAL (32-bit half). DirectDraw calls DriverInit.
; Every section is shared and the base is above 2 GB: Windows 9x then loads the DLL once, into
; the part of the address space all processes see. DirectDraw calls the HAL's functions from
; whichever program uses it, so their addresses must be valid everywhere (otherwise: "Invalid
; 32-bit callback" and no HAL).
LIBRARY RIPPLEDD
EXPORTS
    DriverInit
SECTIONS
    .text  READ EXECUTE SHARED
    .rdata READ SHARED
    .data  READ WRITE SHARED
    .bss   READ WRITE SHARED
    .idata READ WRITE SHARED
    .edata READ SHARED
    .rsrc  READ SHARED
